 Oct 27, 2026 (a Tuesday) would likely start Oct 26th (Sunday) or Oct 27th (Monday) depending on organizational rules. I will define it as the 7 days leading up to and including the current day.\n    *   Start Date: 2026-10-20T00:00:00Z (to capture the full preceding week)\n    *   End Date: 2026-10-31T23:59:59Z (to capture the full following week)\n\n3. Search across all mailboxes for unread/important items within that range.\n4. Since I cannot pass a date range directly to a standard `searchMail` without it being supported by the tool schema (and it only takes `query` and `mailboxId`), I must rely on a flexible query that targets unread status and then filter results in my response, or use `aggregateInbox` and then filter.\n5. Given the complexity and the instruction to \"Work out everything the request needs and search for all of it before you start answering,\" I will use `listMailboxes` and `aggregateInbox` to get a wide, recent view first, as this is the fastest way to give a \"what''s going on\" summary.\n\nLet''s start with `listMailboxes` and `aggregateInbox`.\n`perMailbox` for `aggregateInbox` must be >= 1 and <= 25. I''ll use 10 to get a good sample.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user wants to know what needs their attention across all mailboxes for the current week.\nThis requires checking multiple mailboxes for important or unread/urgent emails.\n\n1.  **Identify the Goal:** Summarize important mail across all connected mailboxes for \"this week\".\n2.  **Determine the Tools:** `aggregateInbox` seems most appropriate for a high-level overview of recent mail across all mailboxes. `searchMail` could be used if \"attention\" implies specific criteria (e.g., unread, high priority, recent).\n3.  **Tool Selection & Refinement:** `aggregateInbox` fetches the most recent inbox emails from EVERY connected mailbox and returns them merged.\n4.  **Time Context:** The user asks for \"this week.\" `aggregateInbox` doesn''t filter by date, it fetches the *mos