lboxes this week?\" and the follow up is \"Which of those is the most urgent?\", I need to determine the most urgent from the list I have.\n\nI will look for deadlines or time-sensitive actions.\nThe Raj Mehta invitation has a specific date/time. It''s an invitation, which typically requires an RSVP.\nThe Harness Bank debit is a transaction notification, which might be urgent if it''s unexpected, but typically is just a notification.\nThe GitHub verification code is time-sensitive (OTP), but usually expires quickly and is handled immediately.\nThe Acme Store shipment is informational.\n\nI will prioritize the **Raj Mehta invitation** because it''s an action item (RSVP) with a specific deadline (Thu Oct 8, 2026, 15:00 UTC).\nI will also mention the **Harness Bank** notification as potentially urgent (financial) and the **GitHub verification code** as time-sensitive, but the invitation is the clearest \"action needed\" item.\n\nLet me check if there''s a way to see if the invitation is accepted or not. I don''t have a tool to read the email body, but the subject line gives a lot of info.\nI will answer based on the provided list. The most urgent is the one requiring a response with a deadline. The \"Rebrand review\" invitation. I will explain my reasoning based on the subject lines."}],"createdAt":1793063937671},{"type":"text","text":"Based on the 10 recent emails from your `ana@harness.test` mailbox, the most urgent one is the **meeting invitation from Raj Mehta** — *Invitation: Rebrand review @ Thu Oct 8, 2026 15:00 UTC* — because it includes a concrete upcoming date and likely requires an RSVP or preparation.\n\nOther items worth watching:\n- **Harness Bank** — *INR 1,250.00 debited from a/c **4821*** — a financial notification; check the amount if you don''t recognise the transaction.\n- **GitHub** — *[GitHub] Your sign-in verification code* — time-sensitive, but usually handled immediately after arrival.\n\nThe remaining emails (Acme Store shipment, Shop Weekly n