INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('2189f1fd-6018-4d46-be34-5ec5cf72cec9','b3d64685-da74-4e2b-af2a-7b3b775f4d8b','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"Thinking Process:\n\n1.  **Analyze the Request:** The user is asking, \"Any money moving out of my accounts lately?\" This is a request for financial/transactional information.\n2.  **Identify Necessary Tools/Capabilities:** I need tools to search for financial transactions, pending payments, or banking/payment activity.\n    *   Available tools are mostly focused on Mail, Calendar, Drive, and Workspace Members.\n    *   *Initial search for relevant tools:* I need to check if any tools related to \"financial transactions,\" \"bank statements,\" \"payments,\" or \"money movement\" are available.\n3.  **Determine Search Strategy (Tool Discovery):** Since this is a financial query, and I don''t see obvious banking tools, I must search my toolset.\n4.  **Formulate Tool Call:** Call `search_tools` with relevant financial keywords.\n5.  **Execute Search and Analyze Results (Self-Correction/Planning):** *Self-correction: Wait until the tools are returned before proceeding.*\n\n*(Self-Correction during the execution phase: If no specific financial tools exist, I must rely on mail/calendar search for evidence of payments (e.g., bills, purchase confirmations) and state the limitation if the information isn''t found there. But first, I must search for specialized financial tools.)*The user is asking about any money moving out of their accounts lately. This implies a need to look for financial transactions, which would likely be found in emails (e.g., bank statements, receipts, payment confirmations) or perhaps related to subscriptions or invoices.\n\nFirst, I need to list all available tools to see if there is a specific \"transaction\" or \"financial\" tool. Then, I''ll search mailboxes for keywords related to money movement, payments, and withdrawals, focusing on recent emails, relative to the turn sent-at of \"2026-10-27T01:23:42.866Z\".\n\nKeywords: \"payment\", \"charged\", \"withdrawal\", \"transaction\", \"money out\", \"invoice\", \"bill\".\nTime range: Since the request is generic (\"lately\"), I will use a reasonable recent window, say the last 30 days, as the user''s relative time window.The user is asking about money moving out of their accounts recently.\nThis requires looking for financial transactions, invoices, or payment confirmations/notifications across all connected mailboxes and potentially Drive files if they contain financial documents (like statements or agreements).\n\n1.  **Identify target information:** Money moving out (payments, transfers, invoices, charges).\n2.  **Determine scope:** \"My accounts\" (all mailboxes/drives).\n3.  **Set timeframe:** \"Lately\" (I will interpret this as the past week relative to the current turn sent-at: 2026-10-27T01:23:42.866Z).\n4.  **Choose tools:** `searchMail` (for emails mentioning payments/charges) and `searchFiles` (for financial documents in drives).\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Execute `searchMail` across all mailboxes for keywords related to money moving out (paid, invoice, charge, payment, transfer, billed, withdrawn).\n2.  Execute `searchFiles` across all drives for financial documents or statements received recently.\n\nSince I don''t know the drive IDs or mailbox IDs for \"my accounts,\" I must start with listing tools if I don''t have the tools loaded, but the instructions say `listMailboxes` and `listDrives` are always available to search for tools/items.\n\nI will search mail first as it''s the most common place for payment confirmations.\n\n**Search Queries:**\n*   **Mail:** `paid OR invoice OR charge OR payment OR transfer OR billed OR withdrawal`\n*   **Files:** `invoice OR statement OR bank statement OR payment receipt OR transaction` (I''ll combine these search patterns into the file search).The user asks: \"Any money moving out of