ail` across all mailboxes for keywords related to money moving out (paid, invoice, charge, payment, transfer, billed, withdrawn).\n2.  Execute `searchFiles` across all drives for financial documents or statements received recently.\n\nSince I don''t know the drive IDs or mailbox IDs for \"my accounts,\" I must start with listing tools if I don''t have the tools loaded, but the instructions say `listMailboxes` and `listDrives` are always available to search for tools/items.\n\nI will search mail first as it''s the most common place for payment confirmations.\n\n**Search Queries:**\n*   **Mail:** `paid OR invoice OR charge OR payment OR transfer OR billed OR withdrawal`\n*   **Files:** `invoice OR statement OR bank statement OR payment receipt OR transaction` (I''ll combine these search patterns into the file search).The user asks: \"Any money moving out of my accounts lately?\" Need to search mail across mailboxes for financial/banking emails — payments, transactions, debits, invoices, subscriptions. The turn clock is 2026-10-27T01:23 UTC. \"Lately\" — maybe last few weeks. Mailbox''s newest message is Sep 26 per earlier aggregate? Actually earlier aggregate showed mailboxes:1 and newest Sep 26. Let me search for financial terms.\n\nI should search across all mailboxes for keywords: \"payment\", \"charged\", \"debit\", \"invoice\", \"receipt\", \"transaction\", \"bank\", \"transfer\", \"subscription\", \"renewal\", \"amount due\".\n\nLet me do multiple searches in one block. Also could call aggregateInbox to get a workspace-wide recent overview. That''s efficient: aggregateInbox perMailbox 25 might reveal financial emails in the recent inbox. But mail may be archived. Search is better.\n\nLet me run several searchMail queries in parallel: \"payment\", \"charged\", \"invoice\", \"receipt\", \"transaction\", \"bank account debit\", \"subscription renewal\". Also \"amount due\".\n\nLet me start with a batch."}],"createdAt":1793064245393},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolI