cmpl-tool-aaa3b8aa004323a7","toolName":"searchMail","args":{"query":"subscription renewal","mailboxId":null}},"updatedAt":1793064249144},{"type":"step-start","createdAt":1793064249149,"model":"openai-compatible.chat/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash:floor"},{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"The user asked, \"Any money moving out of my accounts lately?\"\n\nI performed searches across all connected mailboxes (mailboxId:null) using several keywords related to money moving out:\n1.  `payment` (Returned 50 results from `ana@harness.test`)\n2.  `charged` (0 results)\n3.  `invoice` (0 results)\n4.  `receipt` (0 results)\n5.  `transaction` (0 results)\n6.  `subscription renewal` (0 results)\n\nThe results from `payment` are overwhelmingly internal/technical emails (\"Edge Sender,\" snippets are empty, subjects are generic like \"html-hostile\", \"jsonld-1mb\", \"Re: Long thread\"). None of these indicate a financial transaction or money moving out of a user''s personal/business accounts.\n\nSince the mail search didn''t yield specific financial evidence, I must broaden the search and check the connected drives for financial documents.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1.  List all connected drives to ensure I cover all potential locations for statements or receipts.\n2.  Search all connected drives for financial documents (e.g., \"invoice\", \"bank statement\", \"receipt\", \"payment\").The initial searches for specific payment keywords (`payment`, `charged`, `invoice`, `receipt`, `transaction`, `subscription renewal`) across all mailboxes did not yield any direct results, except for 50 results related to \"Edge Sender\" threads in `ana@harness.test` which appear to be technical/system messages.\n\nThis suggests there are no clear payment confirmations or invoices in the easily searchable keywords.\n\nNow, I should broaden the search to cover more financial terminology and look for specific document types in Drive, which is often where financial statements or downloaded invoices reside.\n\n**