ate a payment or money moving out; they are part of a general thread discussion.\n2.  `charged`: 0 emails found.\n3.  `invoice`: 0 emails found.\n4.  `receipt`: 0 emails found.\n5.  `transaction`: 0 emails found.\n6.  `subscription renewal`: 0 emails found.\n\nNo direct evidence of money moving out or specific financial transactions was found using the primary keywords.\n\n**Next Steps:**\n1.  I should also check Drives for financial documents, as these might be bills or statements the user received.\n2.  I will use `searchFiles` for documents containing financial keywords.\n\n**Plan:**\nExecute `searchFiles` across all drives for: \"invoice\", \"statement\", \"receipt\", \"bank\", \"billing\".\n\nI need to know which drives are connected. I will use `listDrives` first, as it''s always loaded and necessary for the file search. (Although the instructions say I can search every drive, listing them allows me to see if any are present before querying all). I will proceed to list drives.\n\n*Note: If `listDrives` is run, I will then execute `searchFiles` for all returned `driveId`s.*The user asked about money moving out of their accounts lately.\nI performed several searches using `searchMail` across all connected mailboxes for keywords like \"payment\", \"charged\", \"invoice\", \"receipt\", \"transaction\", \"subscription renewal\", and \"amount due\".\n\nAnalysis of Results:\n1.  `payment`: Found 50 results in `ana@harness.test`. (All appear to be technical/Edge Sender messages and snippets are empty/irrelevant to money movement).\n2.  `charged`: Found 0.\n3.  `invoice`: Found 50 in `ana@harness.test`. (Again, all appear to be technical/Edge Sender messages and snippets are empty/irrelevant to money movement. These look like internal system emails or test data.)\n4.  `receipt`: Found 0.\n5.  `transaction`: Found 0.\n6.  `subscription renewal`: Found 0.\n\nConclusion from Mail Search: The email search did not yield any specific, actionable information about personal fi