ands of edge emails). Hmm. The turn clock says \"now\" = 2026-10-27T01:27Z. The inbox top emails are from September 2026 — so no new mail since Sep 26? That''s odd but fine.\n\nI need unread count \"right now\". Options:\n1. searchMail with query \"unread\" or \"is:unread\" — searchMail searches all mailboxes; unknown query semantics but likely full-text/substring search. It may return matches with counts. Could try searchMail query \"is:unread\" — but that''s a query on content, not flags, possibly.\n\nHmm. Perhaps aggregateInbox returns isRead flags for the most recent per mailbox (25). Earlier aggregateInbox gave 25 emails all read. But unread older ones could exist deeper.\n\nBetter: page through listEmails and count unread. But how many pages? The inbox may have ~200+ edge emails. Could be many. Let me try a smarter approach: searchMail might support \"unread\" query? Let''s test searchMail query \"unread\" — risky, it''d match subject text.\n\nAlternative: maybe listEmails supports folder \"inbox\" and there''s an \"unread\" indicator... no.\n\nLet me just page. The nextPageToken \"235\" — pagination. Each page 50. Let''s fetch next pages, counting unread. But this could be 5-10 calls. Inbox seems to be edge-case test mailbox with lots of emails. Perhaps ~200-500 emails.\n\nActually, maybe I can use searchMail with query \"unread\" to see if the tool interprets flags. Let me try searchMail first — one call, might return count. Search \"is:unread\" maybe. If useless, fall back to paging.\n\nLet me do searchMail query \"is:unread\" (mailboxId restricted to this mailbox to avoid duplicates? The default is all mailboxes but there''s only one mailbox).\n\nI''ll try that and simultaneously page the inbox? Dependencies: independent, but paging many calls. Let''s first try searchMail."}],"createdAt":1793064495530},{"type":"tool-invocation","toolInvocation":{"state":"result","result":{"count":0,"emails":[]},"toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-97e6a42f48922174","toolName":"sear