vel folders for each drive. I can call listFolder for each driveId in parallel. That''s 7 calls. Also maybe searchFiles across all drives with a broad query? searchFiles requires a query (min 1 char). Hmm. listFolder for each drive top-level is the cleanest comparison.\n\nLet me call listFolder for all 7 drives in one block.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"The user is asking if all 7 connected drives (`c92b4299-1f7c-571a-ab7e-aa39d6c8bb32`, `66e47377-dba1-5bfd-945e-a2e575ae1511`, `7966bf69-d3ed-5a47-9bd7-9a807d9a645d`, `6b8c0a7c-3d05-5f0c-b50c-e3da0da47f2b`, `1a17bf00-c9d1-5cdd-81d1-ce8b6583982c`, `4258fe0c-92ff-5c5b-85dd-797a798ab5c6`, `a8caddaf-15c9-57c2-a67e-93e7cffc3beb`) contain the same files.\n\nTo answer this, I would need to list the contents (files and folders) of all of them and compare them.\nSince the user is asking about the content of all of them, I must use `search_tools` first, specifically for listing/browsing files across drives.\n\nPlan:\n1. Identify all drive IDs.\n2. Use `search_tools` to list files/folders in the root of each drive.\n3. Compare the results to determine if they are the same.\n\nThe drive IDs are:\n- `c92b4299-1f7c-571a-ab7e-aa39d6c8bb32`\n- `66e47377-dba1-5bfd-945e-a2e575ae1511`\n- `7966bf69-d3ed-5a47-9bd7-9a807d9a645d`\n- `6b8c0a7c-3d05-5f0c-b50c-e3da0da47f2b`\n- `1a17bf00-c9d1-5cdd-81d1-ce8b6583982c`\n- `4258fe0c-92ff-5c5b-85dd-797a798ab5c6`\n- `a8caddaf-15c9-57c2-a67e-93e7cffc3beb`\n\nI will use `search_tools` with a keyword that implies listing or browsing the entire contents of a drive.The user is asking if all connected drives have the same files.\nI have a list of 7 drives:\n1. `c92b4299-1f7c-571a-ab7e-aa39d6c8bb32` (SFTP)\n2. `66e47377-dba1-5bfd-945e-a2e575ae1511` (FTP)\n3. `7966bf69-d3ed-5a47-9bd7-9a807d9a645d` (FTP - folder scoped)\n4. `6b8c0a7c-3d05-5f0c-b50c-e3da0da47f2b` (FTP)\n5. `1a17bf00-c9d1-5cdd-81d1-ce8b6583982c` (WebDAV)\n6. `4258fe0c-92ff-5c5b-85dd-797a798ab5c6` (S3)\n7. `a8caddaf-15c9-57c2-a67e-93e7cffc