o list might include drive items. The phrase \"everything above\" likely means the whole conversation (mail check, member check, workspace state). I have enough. One more consideration: should I check whether the Oct 8 Raj Mehta invite needs a response (pending invitation)? That''s a calendar invitation response — but it''s in the past; the event date passed. I could mention checking with Raj.\n\nI think I have enough to answer. Let me write the prioritized to-do list, being honest about signal quality:\n\nFormat: headline first, then prioritized list P1/P2/P3 with concrete actions, then a \"nothing found\" note on unread mail.\n\nPriorities for this week (Mon Oct 26 – Sun Nov 1, 2026), as of Tue Oct 27 01:32 UTC:\n\n**P1 — Today, Tue Oct 27:** Daily standup 09:00–09:15 UTC (Work calendar). Only hard commitment in the next 5 days besides repeating standups.\n\n**P2 — Rebrand follow-up (Raj Mehta):** \"Rebrand review\" invite was Thu Oct 8 15:00 UTC — already past; kickoff thread Sep 21, no mail since Sep 26. Action: confirm with Raj whether review happened and what''s next. (I can draft that email.)\n\n**P3 — Sunday Nov 1 bulk deadline cluster:** 12 events on the \"Bulk\" calendar, 00:00–20:45 UTC, titles like \"Bulk 168 deadline draft draft\", \"Bulk 0 package invoice deadline\". Verify if real or test data; if real, prep before Sunday.\n\n**P4 — Inbox cleanup:** 100+ edge-case test emails (Sep 10) still sitting in inbox; all read. Archive them.\n\n**Also worth knowing:** 0 unread, 0 workflow runs, 0 pending invites. Nothing to triage.\n\nShould I offer to draft the Raj email or archive? Yes, offer.\n\nLet me double check \"this week\" — the week of Oct 26. Mon Oct 26 standup already passed (it''s 01:32 Tue). So remaining standups: Tue–Fri Oct 27–30.\n\nAlso the \"Daily forever\" edge event duplicates standup — ignore/note as test.\n\nI''ll keep it tight and prioritized.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"I have all the data points now:\n1.  **Mail:** 0 unread emai