INSERT INTO "mastra_messages" ("id","thread_id","content","role","type","createdAt","resourceId") VALUES ('5e199978-a37c-4fba-9c6d-ba2951e50918','b3d64685-da74-4e2b-af2a-7b3b775f4d8b','{"format":2,"parts":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"1. **Analyze the Request:** The user wants to convert a \"to-do list\" into a \"short status update\" suitable for pasting into chat.\n\n2. **Examine Previous Context/Tools:**\n    * The last user request was: \"Find emails that look like newsletters or digests.\"\n    * I executed several tools: `listEvents`, `listWorkflowRuns`, `listInvites`.\n    * The responses from these tools provided calendar and workflow data, *not* a to-do list or a set of actionable tasks (like pending emails).\n    * None of the previous turns established a \"to-do list\" for the AI to process.\n\n3. **Identify the Conflict/Missing Information:**\n    * The user is asking me to turn a \"to-do list\" into a summary, but I have not been provided with any such list.\n    * My last actions provided calendar events, which are not inherently a simple \"to-do list\" ready for chat summarization. They are appointments.\n\n4. **Determine the Necessary Action:** I cannot fulfill the request because I have no to-do list. I need to inform the user of this limitation or, if possible, ask for the list.\n\n5. **Refine Search Strategy (Self-Correction/Precaution):**\n    * Before giving up, I should check if any of my loaded tools could find a \"to-do list\" or \"tasks.\"\n    * Available tools: `listMailboxes`, `aggregateInbox`, `searchMail`, `listCalendars`, `listDrives`.\n    * Capabilities: \"Mail reading,\" \"Mail actions,\" \"Calendar events,\" \"Drive files.\"\n    * *Conclusion:* There is no dedicated \"Task List\" or \"To-Do List\" tool. If a to-do list exists, it would be in an email or a document.\n\n6. **Formulate the Response:**\n    * Since the request is impossible based on the current input, I must state that clearly.\n    * Since the user has been asking for work summaries, perhaps they *mean* the calendar events I just pulled, but I should first ask for clarification before making assumptions.\n    * *Wait*, looking back at the interaction, there was *no* preceding \"to-do list.\"\n    * I will state that I need the list or, if they meant the calendar events from the previous turn, I can summarize those.\n\n7. **Final Plan:** Acknowledge that no explicit to-do list was provided, and ask if they meant the calendar items from the previous turn, or if they intended to provide a list. (However, the AI persona usually attempts to fulfill the request or explain why it can''t. Since I *don''t* have the list, I''ll ask.)\n\n*(Self-Correction on tone: Be direct and helpful, focusing on the missing input.)*\n\n*Execution:* I need to inform the user that no to-do list was provided in the context.The user wants to turn a \"to-do list\" into a short status update for chat.\nHowever, in the previous turn, the user requested to \"Find emails that look like newsletters or digests.\" I did not find a to-do list. I called `listEvents`, `listWorkflowRuns`, and `listInvites` to try and find something related to tasks/schedules, but none of the previous workflow runs or invites were found, and the event list is mostly recurring daily standups and bulk deadlines.\n\nSince no explicit \"to-do list\" was found, and I cannot see a list of tasks, I must ask for clarification or state what I *can* see (the events/deadlines) and if that is what they mean.\n\nGiven the instruction \"Turn that to-do list into a short status update\", it implies I *should* have found one. I must search for emails first, as the original request was about emails.\n\nI will search for emails that look like to-do lists or tasks to see if any recent email content matches a list format, focusing on keywords like \"to do,\" \"list,\" \"tasks,\" \"checklist.\" I need to use `searchMail`.\nI will search all mailboxes (`searchMail`).The user wants to convert a \"to-do list\" into a short status update suitable for a chat.\nHowever, the previous turn was an empty list of events, workflow runs, and invites. I have no \"to-do list\" to turn into a status update.\n\nBefore assuming there is no to-do list, I should check for emails, as that is the primary source of tasks/to-dos in a \"to-do list\" in a workspace context, especially since the previous turn was about finding \"newsletters or digests\" (which often contain to-dos).\n\nPlan:\n1. Call `searchMail` with keywords like \"to-do list\", \"tasks\", \"action items\" across all mailboxes.\n2. If no relevant emails are found, I will state that I could not find any task or to-do list items and therefore cannot create the user''s request.\n\nSince the user has not mentioned a specific to-do list, I must search for one.The user wants to turn a \"to-do list\" into a short status update for chat.\nHowever, the previous turn was \"Find emails that look like newsletters or digests.\" and the tools called were `listEvents`, `listWorkflowRuns`, and `listInvites`. None of these tools are designed to find a \"to-do list,\" and the results of the tools are all calendar/event data, not a to-do list.\n\nThe user''s request is logically disconnected from the action taken (finding newsletters/digests).\nI need to:\n1.  Check if any previous request implied a to-do list that I missed, or if the user is referring to something implicitly found. (No, the previous request was clearly about newsletters/digests).\n2.  Acknowledge the lack of a to-do list and ask for clarification or look for any tasks/reminders in the calendar results that could be construed as a to-do list.\n\nSince the prompt is \"Turn that to-do list into a short status update I could paste into chat\", and there is no list provided or found, I must inform the user.\n\nWait, looking at theThe user wants a short, paste-ready status update version of the to-do list. No tool calls needed — just compress the prior answer into chat-friendly prose. Keep it short. Maybe include the key facts: nothing unread, standup daily, rebrand follow-up overdue, Nov 1 bulk deadlines, inbox cleanup pending.\n\nShould be plain text-ish so it can be pasted into chat. Short paragraphs or a compact bullet list. Avoid markdown tables. Keep tone neutral/professional. Include dates.\n\nLet me draft:\n\n\"Status update — week of Oct 26:\n- Mailbox quiet: 0 unread; newest mail Sep 26. Nothing waiting on me.\n- Schedule: daily standup 09:00 UTC Tue–Fri; no other meetings this week.\n- Open item: Raj Mehta''s rebrand review (Oct 8) has passed with no follow-up — I''m checking in on next steps.\n- Sunday Nov 1: a cluster of bulk deadline/invoice/contract entries on the Bulk calendar — confirming which are real.\n- Housekeeping: ~100 edge-case test emails from Sep 10 queued for archive.\n\nNo blockers.\"\n\nThat''s good. Maybe trim further. Keep \"paste into chat\" — plain, brief. Avoid excessive markdown emphasis? Some bold is fine but pasting into chat usually renders markdown; keep minimal.\n\nI''ll give one compact block.","details":[{"type":"text","text":"1. **Analyze the Request:** The user wants to convert a \"to-do list\" into a \"short status update\" suitable for pasting into chat.\n\n2. **Examine Previous Context/Tools:**\n    * The last user request was: \"Find emails that look like newsletters or digests.\"\n    * I executed several tools: `listEvents`, `listWorkflowRuns`, `listInvites`.\n    * The responses from these tools provided calendar and workflow data, *not* a to-do list or a set of actionable tasks (like pending emails).\n    * None of the previous turns established a \"to-do list\" for the AI to process.\n\n3. **Identify the Conflict/Missing Information:**\n    * The user is asking me to turn a \"to-do list\" into a summary, but I have not been provided with any such list.\n    * My last actions provided calendar events, which are not inherently a simple \"to-do list\" ready for chat summarization. They ar